WEBVTT

c1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
This is Governance, Risk and Controls fundamentals. We cover board responsibilities, legal compliance, and partnership frameworks.

c2
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:18.000
The trust board is the highest governing body. It approves budgets, reviews audits, and sets policy on risk appetite and compliance.

c3
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:28.000
Risk controls are grouped into financial, operational, reputational, and regulatory categories. Each has a designated owner and review cadence.

c4
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:40.000
Legal and Compliance covers the Indian Trusts Act, GST filings, and regulatory reporting requirements. Non-compliance can trigger penalties or loss of tax exemption status.

c5
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:52.000
Internal financial controls compliance is reviewed periodically. The trust board receives transparency and audit compliance reports on a defined schedule.

c6
00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:04.000
Partnerships and alliances are governed by written MOUs. Each partnership is reviewed for legal exposure and reputational alignment before signing.

c7
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:16.000
Key risks monitored include fraud, misallocation of funds, compliance violations, cash losses, and investment risks. Escalation paths are defined in policy.

c8
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:28.000
The governance framework requires periodic statements, transparency reports, and audit compliance reports back to donors, regulators, and the board itself.
